{
  "title": "📋 Trig Values of Standard Angles — The Must-Know Table",
  "hook": "There are five special angles whose trig values you should know by heart: 0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, and 90°. Memorizing this one table unlocks most trigonometry problems!",
  "explanation": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">θ</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">0°</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">30°</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">45°</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">60°</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">90°</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\"><b>sin θ</b></td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">0</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1/2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1/√2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">√3/2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\"><b>cos θ</b></td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">√3/2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1/√2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1/2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">0</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\"><b>tan θ</b></td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">0</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1/√3</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">√3</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">∞ (undefined)</td></tr></table><div style=\"background:#FFF8E1;border-left:4px solid #FFB300;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> <b>Pattern for sin:</b> √0/2, √1/2, √2/2, √3/2, √4/2 → 0, 1/2, 1/√2, √3/2, 1. <b>cos is sin reversed!</b></div><div style=\"background:#E3F2FD;border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">ℹ️ <strong>Tip:</strong> 1/√2 = √2/2 ≈ 0.707.  1/√3 = √3/3 ≈ 0.577.  √3/2 ≈ 0.866.</div><div style=\"background:#F5F5F5;border-left:3px solid #4A90D9;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;margin:6px 0;font-size:0.9rem\">Quick check: sin increases from 0° to 90°. cos decreases from 0° to 90°. tan increases and blows up at 90°.</div>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> Evaluate: 2 sin 30° + 3 cos 60° − tan 45°.<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Substitute values</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">2(1/2) + 3(1/2) − 1</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Compute</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">1 + 3/2 − 1 = 3/2 = 1.5</span></div></div></div><br><b>Example 2:</b> If sin(A + B) = 1 and cos(A − B) = 1, find A and B.<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>sin(A+B) = 1</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">A + B = 90°</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>cos(A−B) = 1</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">A − B = 0° → A = B</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Solve</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">2A = 90° → A = B = 45°</span></div></div></div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "Find the value of: tan²60° + 4cos²45° − 3sec²30° − cot²60°.",
    "hint": "tan 60° = √3, cos 45° = 1/√2, sec 30° = 2/√3, cot 60° = 1/√3.",
    "answer": "(√3)² + 4(1/√2)² − 3(2/√3)² − (1/√3)² = 3 + 4(1/2) − 3(4/3) − 1/3 = 3 + 2 − 4 − 1/3 = 1 − 1/3 = 2/3."
  },
